# Aegis fix catalog #146 — Deployment selector does not match its pod template labels
#
# Tier:       4 · Advanced
# Category:   deploy_failure (auto-diagnosed from the log below)
# Engine:     deterministic rule engine — no AI involved
#
# CI log:
#   | The Deployment "api" is invalid: spec.template.metadata.labels: Invalid value: map[string]string{"app":"shop"}: `selector` does not match template `labels`
#
# How it is solved:
#   MODIFY k8s/deployment.yaml
#     - Aligned pod template labels with the workload selector (Deployment api: template labels now include app: api) — the API server rejects a workload whose spec.selector does not match spec.template.metadata.labels, so kubectl apply fails
#
# Apply:      git apply 04-advanced/146-k8s-selector-mismatch.diff
diff --git a/k8s/deployment.yaml b/k8s/deployment.yaml
--- a/k8s/deployment.yaml
+++ b/k8s/deployment.yaml
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@
   template:
     metadata:
       labels:
-        app: shop
+        app: api
     spec:
       containers:
         - name: api
